/**
 * ============================================================================
 * CLOUDFLARE WORKERS — STATIC ASSETS
 * ============================================================================
 * What `npx wrangler deploy` reads. Without it the deploy command has no idea
 * what to upload and fails.
 *
 * ── Why there is no `main` ────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * A Worker config with `assets` and no `main` is a pure static site: there is
 * no script, nothing executes per request, and Cloudflare serves the files
 * straight from its edge. That is the point. Static asset requests are not
 * metered, so this site costs nothing to serve at any traffic level — whereas
 * a Worker script would put every page view through the (metered) request
 * budget for no benefit, since all 42 pages are already prerendered HTML.
 *
 * Adding `main` later is what you would do to run server code. Do not add it
 * to "make routing work" — routing is handled below.
 *
 * ── html_handling: why drop-trailing-slash ───────────────────────────────
 * The export writes `out/tools/merge-pdf.html`. Visitors, the sitemap and the
 * `<link rel="canonical">` on every page all say `/tools/merge-pdf`, with no
 * trailing slash.
 *
 * `drop-trailing-slash` makes that exact URL serve the file with a 200, and
 * redirects `/tools/merge-pdf/` to it. The default, `auto-trailing-slash`,
 * would also work, but this states the intent: one canonical spelling per
 * page. Two URLs serving identical content is the duplicate-content problem
 * that splits a page's ranking signals between them.
 *
 * ── not_found_handling: why 404-page and not SPA ─────────────────────────
 * `404-page` serves `out/404.html` with a real 404 status for anything that
 * does not exist. `single-page-application` would return `index.html` with a
 * 200 instead — which for this site would be a disaster: every mistyped URL
 * would look to Google like another copy of the homepage, and a crawler would
 * index dozens of soft-404s. This site is not an SPA; it is 37 real documents.
 *
 * ── _headers ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * Security headers, the CSP and the cache policy come from `public/_headers`,
 * which the export copies to `out/_headers`. Wrangler picks it up from the
 * assets directory automatically — it is not referenced here.
 * ============================================================================
 */
{
  "name": "toolzen",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-10",
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./out",
    "html_handling": "drop-trailing-slash",
    "not_found_handling": "404-page"
  }
}
